  "scope": "RFC 9530 Want-Content-Digest and Want-Repr-Digest request/response header admission, preserving hint semantics and independent integrity enforcement. Local simulated peers and loopback tests only.",
  "standards": [
    "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9530.html#section-4",
    "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8941.html#section-4.2.2",
    "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8941.html#section-4.2.4"
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Validate both independent preference dictionaries and integer weights 0 through 10 before request inspection/dispatch and response delivery, including raw/interim/bodyless paths and the direct Go client.",
    "Reuse the existing RFC 8941 key and opaque-parameter grammar across all four integrity/preference fields; preserve the 1024-member, 256-parameter and existing byte/field ceilings.",
    "Accept an empty dictionary, leading zeros, negative zero, unknown algorithm preferences and ordinary parameters; reject wrong numeric types/ranges, malformed values and duplicate algorithm keys.",
    "Do not require an actual digest, choose an algorithm, enforce peer compliance with hints or waive actual digest checks based on preferences.",
    "Preserve repeated case-variant preference fields in Python output, reject empty internal value arrays, protect both fields from Connection nomination and keep MIME field semantics separate.",
    "No new Snort SID or deployment change."
  ],
